From d9c6c45b10b86eb78255b0e1ae8599bfdd6bc158 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "T. Kurt Bond" <tkurtbond@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:18:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 41/48] MathL.small: the smallest normal LONGREAL

Needs "Accept real literals below the smallest normal number" (and so
the two fixes it needs) to compile, and "Write real constants to C
exactly" for the value to reach the C code exactly.

small was 2.2250738585072014/9.9999999999999981D307, a workaround for
the scanner refusing 2.2250738585072014D-308, and the C written for it
was 0, so MathL.small was 0.0. With the constants written exactly the
quotient is 000FFFFFFAAD8B05, a denormal, still not 2^-1022. small is
now the literal 2.2250738585072014D-308, which is 2^-1022 exactly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/runtime/MathL.Mod | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/runtime/MathL.Mod b/src/runtime/MathL.Mod
index f6da1527..74d1f4c0 100644
--- a/src/runtime/MathL.Mod
+++ b/src/runtime/MathL.Mod
@@ -86,8 +86,7 @@
 
   places*   = 53;
   large*    = MAX(LONGREAL); (*1.7976931348623157D+308;*)  (* MAX(LONGREAL) *)
-(*small*    = 2.2250738585072014D-308; *)
-  small*    = 2.2250738585072014/9.9999999999999981D307(*/10^308)*);
+  small*    = 2.2250738585072014D-308;  (* 2^-1022, the smallest normal LONGREAL *)
   expoMax*  = 1023;
   expoMin*  = 1-expoMax;
   expOffset = expoMax;
-- 
2.55.0

